    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "coverage_text",
      "x": 84,
      "y": 1382,
      "width": 1232,
      "height": 256,
      "text": "Installed Plugin Coverage\\n\\nMapped directly in this config: which-key.nvim, conform.nvim, todo-comments.nvim, oil.nvim, codecompanion.nvim, agentic.nvim, augment.vim, gitsigns.nvim, snacks.nvim, solarized.nvim, mcphub.nvim, code-preview.nvim, claudecode.nvim, opencode.nvim, codex.nvim, nvim-gemini-companion, trouble.nvim, overseer.nvim, neotest, neotest-python, neotest-vitest, neotest-golang, neotest-rust, nvim-dap, nvim-dap-ui.\\n\\nInstalled with no explicit top-level keymaps here: blink.cmp, fidget.nvim, friendly-snippets, lazy.nvim, lazydev.nvim, lualine.nvim, mason.nvim, mason-lspconfig.nvim, mason-nvim-dap.nvim, mini.pairs, mini.surround, nvim-lspconfig, nvim-nio, nvim-treesitter, nvim-web-devicons, plenary.nvim, ts-comments.nvim.\\n\\nTakeaway: explicit keys are concentrated in editing, IDE, and AI surfaces; the remaining plugins are automatic support, dependency, or UI infrastructure.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "coverage_box",
      "originalText": "Installed Plugin Coverage\\n\\nMapped directly in this config: which-key.nvim, conform.nvim, todo-comments.nvim, oil.nvim, codecompanion.nvim, agentic.nvim, augment.vim, gitsigns.nvim, snacks.nvim, solarized.nvim, mcphub.nvim, code-preview.nvim, claudecode.nvim, opencode.nvim, codex.nvim, nvim-gemini-companion, trouble.nvim, overseer.nvim, neotest, neotest-python, neotest-vitest, neotest-golang, neotest-rust, nvim-dap, nvim-dap-ui.\\n\\nInstalled with no explicit top-level keymaps here: blink.cmp, fidget.nvim, friendly-snippets, lazy.nvim, lazydev.nvim, lualine.nvim, mason.nvim, mason-lspconfig.nvim, mason-nvim-dap.nvim, mini.pairs, mini.surround, nvim-lspconfig, nvim-nio, nvim-treesitter, nvim-web-devicons, plenary.nvim, ts-comments.nvim.\\n\\nTakeaway: explicit keys are concentrated in editing, IDE, and AI surfaces; the remaining plugins are automatic support, dependency, or UI infrastructure.",
